        "problem": "Solve the inequality $6-\\sqrt[3]{10+3x}<2.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
        "worked_solution": "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-\\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & <2 \\\\ -\\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & <-4 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{10+3x})}^{3} & >{4}^{3} \\\\ 10+3x & >64 \\\\ 3x & >54 \\\\ x & >18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
